side here but talking here  um for our state of Nevada we're seeing  this thing called the superbug  um and it's really kind of uh we're  seeing just a an uptick here in cases  almost uh 800 cases 63 deaths here  um what should people know about this  well this superbug is called Canada orus  it's a fungus  that belongs to a family of fungi that's  usually pretty benign this is a fungus  that many of us have in our bodies and  we never notice it or it can cause in  some people a an inflammation of the  esophagus you know the the the feeding  tube and back in the throat and  occasionally it can cause in women a  vaginal uh infection so usually pretty  benign but this variant which has  cropped up in several parts of the world  is more ferocious it generally hovers  around hospitals infecting people who  are otherwise already very ill and  receiving antibiotics  it can be out in the environment and it  when it infects these people it can get  into their bloodstream and cause other  infections in organ systems and to make  the challenge even greater it's often  somewhat difficult to treat because it  can be resistant to some of the  anti-fungal drugs that we usually use so  it's challenging and it's cropped up  here in the United States starting in  2016 in hospitals Here There and  Everywhere  but there is treatment we should mention  that right  there is treatment we have other  anti-fungal agents and when patients are  infected they are put in their private  rooms in isolation and healthcare  workers wear gowns and gloves caring for  them so they won't spread it to others  and there's a lot of intensive  disinfection of the inanimate  environment around them so a lot of good  infection control usually coordinated  with the local public health department  all right good information there for for  our viewers all right so jumping back a  little bit  um I want to go back to covid um talking  about the boosters right now so many  people are kind of like on on the fence 