y difficulty breathing  please take them to a health care  provider very very quickly they can be  taken care of  pediatricians know how to help children  through this infection and almost all of  them come out on the other side  perfectly fine  and Doctor also um Health officials here  today they're they uh they made an  announcement here that we have a code  red for hospital beds basically just  over capacity here uh in Nevada uh which  what what does this all mean here for  residents moving forward  well what's happening across the country  not only in Nevada is that these three  viruses are really straining Health Care  Systems  around here we have lots of infection  and we're working very hard but we  haven't been overwhelmed yet it does  mean that Health Systems have to provide  longer coverage more people out there  people are working longer and they may  have to adjust actually the sorts of  patients that are admitted to hospitals  for a while for example people who are  scheduled for elective procedures they  find that they have to postpone those  because we need those beds for people  who are acutely ill  and then one last question doctor Before  I Let You Go  um you know just overall just the  primary way here to stay safe  um but get your vaccines I mean are you  also recommending maybe just kind of  bring that mask back up especially  during um the holidays when people are  starting to gather here to celebrate  well Christian I'm so glad you asked  because there are some things we can do  to protect ourselves our families and  our communities  fundamental is getting vaccinated and  I'm talking about two vaccines the covet  booster everyone five and older is  eligible for that and the regular  seasonal influenza vaccine everyone's  six months of age and older is  recommended to receive that both of  those vaccines can help prevent the  serious complications of those  infections and I recognize we're asking  people to roll up both their sleeves  coveted and flu but it's very important  number two good hand hygiene that RSV  can get on your fingers then if you  touch your nose or your mouth you can  infect yourself so frequent hand hygiene  if you do become ill  contact your health care provider I  didn't say go because you don't want to  spread it to everyone in the waiting  room but contact them because we have  treatments particularly for covid and  for influenza that can ameliorate the  severity of those infections  and particularly for people at high risk  of the complications of both these  viruses older people people who are have  have underlying illnesses heart disease  lung disease diabetes people who are  immune compromised dust off that mask  put it back on when you go out into  crowds and that includes the mall if  you're going shopping  social distancing may be a good idea I  know you'd like to go to all those  parties but if you really have an  underlying illness  think about it twice maybe it's time to  stream a movie rather than rent a movie  yeah it's also a very good time to maybe  show off that holiday spirit with the  mass you can always obviously just  decorate it there but you could give a  reminder here for viewers is there a  risk of getting the covet booster shot  and the flu at the same time or do you  recommend just kind of getting them uh  in different dates you can actually get  them both at the same time no harm  except yes both arms may be sore for a  day or two but other than that there's  no contraindication to getting them both  at the same time  if you want to spread them out please  make an early New Year's resolution to  absolutely get that second dose because  you know a vaccine deferred is often  unfortunately a vaccine that was never  received so uh  uh you know a bird in the hand is worth  two in the bush so get them at the same  time  all right thank you so much Dr shaffner  thank you so much for your time we  appreciated anything else that you want  to uh add that I forgot to ask we're  comprehensive here Christian thank you  thank you so much I appreciate it

